  "desc": "Cells tracks (病理 C2) never interpolate: a keyframe carries a whole ROI's cells in instances[] (each = bbox + bbox-local RLE + class + score), and a segment touching an instances-bearing keyframe HOLDS the start keyframe wholesale. Dispatch is by geometry PRESENCE not kind — cells' rle is nested inside instances so the top-level rle/bbox are empty; without an explicit instances guard, InterpolateAt would fall into lerpGeom and silently drop every cell (CLAUDE.md #6). Mid-segment queries must return kf0's instances verbatim; the second keyframe takes over only at its own ts.",
